    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Build Your Dynamic List\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Fetch your API data and render your sketched card layout dynamically.\r\n\r\n1. **Create Your Async Function:** Write an async function that requests data from your API.\r\n2. **Await the Response:** Use await so your app waits for the data before rendering.\r\n3. **Store the Data:** Save the returned data in a variable you can loop over.\r\n4. **Render with .map():** Use .map() to generate one card per item using your sketched layout.\r\n5. **Insert into the DOM:** Display the generated cards inside your container element.\r\n\r\n**Optional:** If you see undefined errors, log the data inside your .map() to confirm property names match your API response.",
